# E-commerce User Funnel Analysis

## Overview
This project analyzes e-commerce user behavior based on event-level data. 
The goal is to understand user activity, acquisition channels, device usage, and conversion funnel performance.

## Tools
- Python
- Pandas
- Matplotlib
- Google Colab

## Dataset
The dataset contains user interaction events, including:
- user activity
- session data
- device information
- marketing channel
- user funnel events

## Analysis Performed

### 1. Active Users by Country
Analyzed the most active countries during Q2 2025 based on unique users.

### 2. Monthly Active Users by Channel
Compared user activity trends across different acquisition channels.

### 3. Device Usage Analysis
Identified the most frequently used devices based on unique sessions.

### 4. Search-to-Add-to-Cart Conversion
Measured the percentage of users who moved from product search to adding items to cart.

## Key Insights
- Country X had the highest number of active users in Q2 2025.
- Channel performance varied across months.
- Mobile devices contributed the highest number of sessions.
- Search-to-add-to-cart conversion rate was XX%.

## Recommendation
Improving user experience on high-traffic channels and optimizing mobile shopping flow may help increase conversion.
